Eva pours coffee into two large cups.
We sit down on the soft sofa in the living room.
"How are things going for you in the city now?" Eva asks.
I take a sip of the warm coffee.
I tell her that I feel that my new life is actually really lovely.
"I have finally settled in well here," I say with a smile.
"I am glad to hear that," she replies.
"You also work really hard on our project at the office."
"Yes, but I intend to take more time off now," I say.
"I will enjoy the city much more on the weekends."
"I understand that well," Eva says.
We talk for a long time about our other colleagues and the work.
The atmosphere is very cozy and relaxed.
I smile at her over the coffee cup.
I say that I hope that we will still see each other outside of work.
"We definitely will," she answers happily.
I think that we probably will have many fun evenings together.
